# MacBook -> mini — the MacBook's dedicated OUTBOUND key into the mini, so every
# ssh to the mini (interactive, scripts, rd, herdr-core's machine link from a
# launchd job with no SSH_AUTH_SOCK) works with no 1Password prompt. Mirror of
# config/ssh/authorized_keys.iumac, reversed: it must be installed on the mini
# ONLY, never on the MacBook, which holds the matching PRIVATE key on disk
# (~/.ssh/id_ed25519_mini, mode 600, never in git). Installing the public half
# on the MacBook too would let that private key authenticate back into it.
#
# `make authorized-keys` enforces the split with the same backend marker
# (`${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-$HOME/.config}/secrets/backend`, "cache" = the mini) as
# the .iumac file, inverted: installed when backend == cache, skipped elsewhere.
#
# `restrict,pty,port-forwarding`: plain `ssh mini` forwards no agent (see
# `Host mini`; `mini-fwd` authenticates with the 1Password key, not this one), so
# agent/X11/user-rc stay off. `pty` keeps interactive shells, `port-forwarding`
# keeps the -L tunnels (db-tunnel, dev ports). Exec, scp/rsync, ControlMaster and
# herdr-core's `connect` need nothing more. No `from=`: source restriction is the
# tailnet ACL's job (tag:mac, and tag:phone for the line below, reach tcp:22), and a Tailscale IP must not
# enter git.
# An install is append-if-missing: replace the old bare line by hand when this
# one changes (the old unrestricted line would otherwise sit beside it).
restrict,pty,port-forwarding ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIFV6VLkwTt7YVwApTOgd7bMOIa1+F8Fk1jftN0sSMOsG macbook->mini

# iPhone -> mini — the Herdr phone app's key (generated on the phone, private half in its
# iOS Keychain). `restrict,pty`: a shell and herdr-core's connect, no forwarding of any
# kind. Reached through the tag:phone -> tag:devhost tcp:22 grant (dotfiles-private).
restrict,pty ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHF+lTrT7v78ma4daC7EAkLJtstz0lM/l+r7ZNFwrO2L iphone-herdr->mini
